@startuml config_reload
'
' Engineered by  Christian Schnapka
'                Embedded Principal+ Engineer
'                Macstab GmbH · Hamburg, Germany
'                https://macstab.com
'
' Two-snapshot CAS reload of the rule file.
' Shows the 1 ms throttle, the change-stamp state machine, the
' CAS winner path and the loser path (no waiting: losers serve the
' active snapshot).
'
' Reference: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md "Config Reloading", docs/PLATFORM.md §12
'            src/config/chaos_io_config.c and src/*/chaos_*_config.c
'            (every library uses the same protocol)
'
title Two-Snapshot CAS Config Reload — Winner and Loser Threads

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 4
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor                 #2C3E50
  LifeLineBorderColor        #2C3E50
  LifeLineBackgroundColor    #ECF0F1
  ParticipantBorderColor     #2C3E50
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontStyle       bold
  GroupBackgroundColor       #FDFEFE
  GroupBorderColor           #95A5A6
}
hide footbox

participant "Thread A\n(reload winner)" as A
participant "cached_mtime\n(volatile uint64)" as Slot
participant "Snapshots\n(2 static buffers\n+ active index)" as Store
participant "Thread B\n(concurrent caller)" as B

note over Slot
  State encoding:
  MISSING    = 0x0000…0000  (no file at the last look)
  UNKNOWN    = 0xffff…ffff  (before the first load)
  RELOADING  = 0xffff…fffe  (reload claimed)
  <stamp>    = hash(mtime s+ns, size, inode, dev);
               a hash equal to a sentinel is XORed
               with 0x9e3779b97f4a7c15
end note

== Every intercepted call: prepare() ==

A -> Slot : atomic load
note right of A
  Throttle: skip the look if the last look was
  < 1 ms ago (vDSO CLOCK_MONOTONIC, chaos_clock.h).
  Never skipped while UNKNOWN or RELOADING;
  always looks when no vDSO clock exists.
  When not skipped, due hits are flushed first.
end note
A -> A : stat(rule file) → observed\n(under the guard; errno restored by prepare())
A -> Slot : atomic load → cached
note right of A
  observed == cached, load not provisional
  (and, io only, no link re-check due):
  nothing to do, serve the active snapshot.
end note
A -> Slot : CAS(cached, RELOADING)
note right of Slot
  __sync_bool_compare_and_swap:
  exactly one thread wins. A loser
  serves the active snapshot.
end note

== Thread B meets the claim ==

B -> Slot : atomic load → RELOADING
B -> Store : __sync_synchronize(); load active index
note right of B
  No wait, no spin: B serves this call from
  the snapshot that is still active. The
  winner publishes shortly; B's next call
  sees the new rules.
end note
B -> Store : copy rule; seqlock check of the copy
note right of B
  sequence read before and after the copy;
  odd or changed → copy discarded,
  the call passes through once
end note

== Thread A: winner reloads ==

A -> Store : inactive.sequence odd (write_begin), clear inactive
A -> Store : open + read rule file into the static 256 KiB buffer\n(raw syscalls; libchaos-io: real open/read under the guard)
A -> Store : fstat(fd): stamp still == observed?
alt transient failure (open/read error other than EACCES/EPERM/EISDIR,\nfile changed during the read), or provisional re-read with identical content
  A -> Slot : __sync_synchronize(); store previous stamp
  note right of Slot
    Active snapshot kept (with hit counts
    and @first claims); claim released;
    the next look retries.
  end note
else read complete (or file missing, or rejected as a whole)
  A -> Store : parse into inactive (all or nothing),\nattach hit slots, write status file, release slots of rules that left
  A -> Store : sequence even (write_end)
  A -> Store : __sync_synchronize(); active index = inactive;\n__sync_synchronize()
  A -> Slot : store observed stamp (claim released)
  note right of Slot
    Index before stamp: a thread that sees the
    new stamp also sees the new index.
    Nothing is allocated or freed: the old
    snapshot becomes the next reload's target.
  end note
end

@enduml
